# Vendored sliver binaries are a local cache - too large for git (283 MB exe,
# GitHub's 100 MB/file limit). The Dockerfile bind-mounts this dir when it
# exists and falls back to a SHA256-pinned download from GitHub releases.
*
!Dockerfile
!bootstrap.sh
!bootrc.rc
!.dockerignore
# The Dockerfile's `RUN --mount=type=bind,source=bin` FAILS at build time when
# the source directory does not exist, which it never does on a fresh clone
# (everything here is ignored above). Keeping the directory in git via a
# placeholder is what makes the documented download fallback reachable.
!bin/
bin/*
!bin/.gitkeep
